// official-intraday-breaks-1 — replica of https://echarts.apache.org/examples/zh/editor.html?c=intraday-breaks-1
// title: Intraday Chart with Breaks / titleCN: 断轴上的日内走势图
// A 4-day minute-by-minute price line on a `time` xAxis whose overnight gaps (16:00 → next 09:30 UTC)
// are collapsed by ECharts 6 axis BREAKS, so only trading hours consume x-space. Each session ends
// with a null point so the line does not bridge the break; `dataZoom` (inside + slider) can widen a
// break back out.
//
// DEVIATIONS from the official source:
//   - DATA INLINED. The official `generateData()` is a `Math.random()` walk (upstream itself labels it
//     "not relevant to echarts API"), so the two panes would show different lines and the diff would be
//     worthless. It was re-run once with a seeded PRNG (mulberry32, seed 20) and the result frozen into
//     the JSON below, which BOTH panes read — the web pane splices the same text, so the lines are
//     identical by construction. Same seed range as upstream (open 1669, drifting ~1440–1800).
//     Dropping the generator also drops its TypeScript type annotations (`time: Date`), which would be
//     a SyntaxError in the reference pane's classic script.
//   - `NaN` → `null` in the inlined data. JSON cannot carry NaN; echarts treats a null value the same
//     (an empty point that breaks the line), which is all the upstream `NaN` is there for.
//   - The now-unused `roundTime` / `BREAK_GAP` vars (only ever read by `generateData`) are dropped.
//   - Native pane: xAxis.axisLabel.formatter omitted (JS closure) — see PORT-NOTE.
